# mcp-execute-missing-command - ze_execute called with no command fails closed
# with a clear argument error.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-mcp2026-1-stateless-core AC-15, on the branch Phase 2 left
# intact. This client declares NO elicitation capability (no --elicit flag), so
# askForCommand (internal/component/mcp/mrtr.go) takes the fail-closed path: the
# call returns HTTP 200 with a tool-level error naming the missing argument, and
# no elicitation/create frame is produced.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-07-30: the header used to say `command` is required
# "unconditionally now ... for anyone", which was written when Phase 1 had
# deleted elicitation. Phase 2 restored it as Multi Round-Trip Requests, so a
# client that DOES declare form mode is prompted instead -- see
# mcp-mrtr-elicit-roundtrip.ci. Only the no-capability branch is this test's
# subject, and that is the branch the absence of --elicit selects.
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY: this file was elicitation-no-capability.ci, and its
# subject was capability NEGOTIATION -- it proved the server did not prompt a
# client that had not declared capabilities.elicitation at initialize. MCP
# 2026-07-28 removed both halves of that: there is no initialize handshake to
# declare a capability at, and a server may no longer send an independent
# JSON-RPC request on any stream, so there is no round trip left to prompt on.
# Every client is now a no-prompt client, which makes this the canonical test
# for the one behavior that remains: the missing argument is reported, not
# waited on. The test body is unchanged because it was always driving the branch
# that survived; only what it means changed.
#
# PREVENTS: a caller hanging on a prompt that can never arrive, and a silent
# dispatch of an empty command string. The failure must be immediate, named, and
# on the response the caller is already waiting for.

stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
@ze_execute {"command":""}
EOF_MCP

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze --mcp $PORT -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test mcp --port $PORT:stdin=mcp:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=1
# pattern= rather than contains= because the needle carries a colon, and a
# contains= value is split on it (ci.ParseKVPairs) -- which would silently
# shorten this to "missing required argument" and stop proving WHICH argument.
expect=stderr:pattern=missing required argument: command
# The error is a TOOL-level error on a normal 200 response, not a transport
# refusal: the request itself was conformant and only its arguments were wrong.
expect=stderr:contains=command error
reject=stdout:contains=elicitation/create
# reject=stderr takes a regex, not contains= (parseReject, record_parse.go):
# a contains= here parses as an empty pattern and is a hard parse error.
reject=stderr:pattern=elicitation/create
